## Contract

Static array-based stack with fixed capacity (128 elements). No dynamic memory allocation. All operations return success/failure indicators.

### Functions

| Function | Parameters | Returns | Failure |
|----------|------------|---------|---------|
| `stack_init` | `struct StaticStack* s` | `void` | — |
| `stack_push` | `struct StaticStack* s, int val` | `int` (1=success, 0=failure) | Stack overflow (top >= CAPACITY-1) |
| `stack_pop` | `struct StaticStack* s, int* out` | `int` (1=success, 0=failure) | Stack underflow (top < 0) |
| `stack_peek` | `struct StaticStack* s, int* out` | `int` (1=success, 0=failure) | Stack underflow (top < 0) |
| `stack_is_empty` | `struct StaticStack* s` | `int` (1=empty, 0=non-empty) | — |

### Struct

```c
struct StaticStack {
    int data[STACK_CAPACITY];
    int top;       // -1 when empty
};
```

## Dependencies

- `array-base` — base skill for array conventions

## Prohibitions

- `malloc`, `calloc`, `realloc`, `free` — no dynamic memory

## Boundaries

- Capacity: 128 elements (STACK_CAPACITY)
- Index range: 0 to CAPACITY-1
- top: -1 (empty) to CAPACITY-1 (full)

## Examples

```c
struct StaticStack s;
stack_init(&s);

stack_push(&s, 10);   // 1
stack_push(&s, 20);   // 1
stack_push(&s, 30);   // 1

int val;
stack_peek(&s, &val); // 1, val=30
stack_pop(&s, &val);  // 1, val=30
stack_pop(&s, &val);  // 1, val=20
stack_pop(&s, &val);  // 1, val=10
stack_pop(&s, &val);  // 0 (underflow)
stack_is_empty(&s);   // 1
```

```c
// Full stack
for (int i = 0; i < 128; i++) stack_push(&s, i);  // 1
stack_push(&s, 999);                              // 0 (overflow)
```

[code]
```c
#define STACK_CAPACITY 128

struct StaticStack {
    int data[STACK_CAPACITY];
    int top;
};

void stack_init(struct StaticStack* s) {
    s->top = -1;
}

int stack_push(struct StaticStack* s, int val) {
    if (s->top >= STACK_CAPACITY - 1) return 0;
    s->data[++s->top] = val;
    return 1;
}

int stack_pop(struct StaticStack* s, int* out) {
    if (s->top < 0) return 0;
    *out = s->data[s->top--];
    return 1;
}

int stack_peek(struct StaticStack* s, int* out) {
    if (s->top < 0) return 0;
    *out = s->data[s->top];
    return 1;
}

int stack_is_empty(struct StaticStack* s) {
    return s->top < 0;
}
```
[/code]
